    "narrative": "The lineup for LawDog today leans heavily into favorable matchups against middle-tier arms to drive efficiency across our 5x5 categories. **Geraldo Perdomo** (67.55) and **Tyler Freeman** (67.23) stand as our strongest plays; **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits significantly from a favorable SP_xERA of 5.15 and a prime spot in the three-hole, while **Tyler Freeman** capitalizes on high-upside placement at the top of the order against a beatable arm in Rodriguez. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (66.16) remains an auto-start despite the tough matchup, as his elite contact profile and lineup position consistently mitigate the risks posed by Mize. We are banking on this trio to anchor our counting stats while maintaining the batting average stability required to stay competitive.\n\nOur most critical bench decision involved **Lawrence Butler** (54.21), who just narrowly squeezed into the starting lineup over the remaining depth. While **Lawrence Butler** is suppressed by a #9 spot in the order, his platoon advantage against Soriano provides enough of a statistical ceiling to warrant his inclusion over our less favorable alternatives. We are closely monitoring the status of **Cal Raleigh**, who remains sidelined on the IL, alongside our other bench assets like **Will Smith**, **Bryson Stott**, and **Taylor Ward**, all of whom are unavailable due to scheduling. We\u2019ve had to make do without the contributions of **Yainer Diaz**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Matt Chapman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Gavin Sheets**, and **Drew Gilbert** today, as their lack of favorable daily projections necessitates a disciplined approach to our game caps.\n\nRisks today are moderate but worth noting for the late-game stretch. **Daulton Varsho** (57.29) carries a volatile score due to a tough platoon disadvantage against Rod\u00f3n, requiring us to pay close attention to his early-game plate appearances. Furthermore, while **Masyn Winn** (41.87) is active, his matchup against Ashcraft is our lowest-scoring start of the day, reflecting both a difficult pitching environment and the defensive prowess of the opposing battery. We are playing for consistent production today, prioritizing the high floor of our top-ranked infielders while keeping a close eye on weather developments that could impact the run-scoring environments for **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Tyler Freeman**.",
